WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.350
Hi, welcome back to Arya Nagarjuna.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.570
And we are still in the
middle of this tough,

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.200
it became a tough chapter, right?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.809
A chapter about investigating karma.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.033
And we thought that we were going

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.199
to have a normal discussion, but

00:00:14.199 --> 00:00:17.430
it's already gone off
on some difficult parts.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.960
And by the way, now Nagarjuna,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.469
having given the Abhidharma version of,

00:00:23.469 --> 00:00:25.908
what do we call it, don't lose it?

00:00:25.908 --> 00:00:26.741
- [Student] Don't go away.

00:00:26.741 --> 00:00:27.697
- Don't go aways.

00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:31.426
He's going, now he is going to give

00:00:31.426 --> 00:00:34.760
a more standard Madhyamika discussion.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:35.726
Here we go.

00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:37.888
The next verse says,

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:39.454
,GAL TE LAS LA RANG BZHIN YOD,

00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:41.229
,RTAG PAR 'GYUR BAR THE TSOM MED,

00:00:41.229 --> 00:00:43.229
,LAS NI BYAS PA MA YIN 'GYUR,

00:00:43.229 --> 00:00:46.066
,RTAG LA BYA BA MED PHYIR RO,

00:00:46.066 --> 00:00:49.200
GAL TE LAS LA RANG BZHIN YOD

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.360
And karma, the laws of karma,

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.300
are something that you
and me feel instinctively.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.280
We just talked, we had a discussion here

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.690
about it with our friends.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.470
It feels like they are self-existent.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.740
It feels like those laws are unbreakable,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.440
cannot be changed,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.240
and they come from their own side.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.470
Like, I understand that in general

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:13.030
things are coming from me.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.300
But who made the laws of the universe?

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.428
Who made the laws of karma?

00:01:18.428 --> 00:01:20.456
And so Nargarjuna is going
to try to convince us

00:01:20.456 --> 00:01:24.550
that our karma made the laws of karma.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.820
And that just because laws of
karma are coming from karma,

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.450
doesn't mean they could work differently

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.995
then the way they do.

00:01:31.995 --> 00:01:34.570
Just because something is empty,

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.370
doesn't mean that it will come

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.742
in a thousand different forms.

00:01:39.742 --> 00:01:42.840
All right, GAL TE LAS LA RANG BZHIN YOD

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.747
If karma itself, if the laws
of karma had their own nature,

00:01:46.747 --> 00:01:48.516
RTAG PAR 'GYUR BAR THE TSOM MED

00:01:48.516 --> 00:01:53.349
there's no doubt that it
would be unchanging -- RTAG PA

00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:56.540
If karma were coming from its own side,

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.115
it would never vary.

00:01:58.115 --> 00:01:59.948
It would always stay the same.

00:01:59.948 --> 00:02:03.482
It would be unchanging.

00:02:03.482 --> 00:02:05.431
LAS NI BYAS PA MA YIN 'GYUR

00:02:05.431 --> 00:02:06.650
If something is unchanging,

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:11.500
it cannot have involved an agent.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.027
If karma, if anything in the universe

00:02:15.027 --> 00:02:19.359
is unchanging, that means nobody did it.

00:02:19.359 --> 00:02:21.880
Because if somebody did
it, then it would change

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.880
because the effects of doing
something get less over time.

00:02:27.521 --> 00:02:29.100
Things fall apart.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.440
That famous book title
"Things Fall Apart",

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.642
that's the nature of things.

00:02:33.642 --> 00:02:37.080
So if things are created, they fall apart.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.300
If things don't fall apart,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.383
then they can not have had

00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:43.124
someone create them.

00:02:43.124 --> 00:02:46.746
Got it? That's all right, right?

00:02:46.746 --> 00:02:50.262
LAS NI BYAS PA MA YIN 'GYUR

00:02:50.262 --> 00:02:52.620
And RTAG LA BYA BA MED PHYIR RO.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.520
If something is unchanging,

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.650
there cannot have been a process
of creation at the beginning of it.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.010
Because the process of creation,

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.388
the process of pushing
something into being,

00:03:04.388 --> 00:03:09.388
that energy which pushes the thing
into being is lost over time.

00:03:10.043 --> 00:03:11.180
So if it's unchanging,

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.900
if karma has a nature of
its own, from its own side,

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:16.750
it's unchanging.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.270
If it's unchanging, it cannot have had

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.012
the person who committed the karma.

00:03:23.012 --> 00:03:24.550
No one made the karma.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.292
Got it?

00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:28.530
All right.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.085
And I think of it as a driverless car.

00:03:33.235 --> 00:03:35.920
And that used to be a
real serious argument,

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.706
but now we do have driverless cars.

00:03:39.706 --> 00:03:43.557
So I want to say a driverless
car without a program.

00:03:44.582 --> 00:03:47.570
A car driving itself without the internet.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.950
How is that? For now.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.120
I don't know what's coming later.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.224
Next verse.

00:03:54.974 --> 00:03:56.682
,CI STE LAS NI MA BYAS NA,

00:03:56.682 --> 00:03:58.624
,MA BYAS PA DANG PHRAD 'JIGS 'GYUR,

00:03:58.624 --> 00:04:01.432
,TSANGS SPYOD GNAS PA MA YIN PA'ANG,

00:04:01.432 --> 00:04:03.573
,DE LA SKYON DU THAL BAR 'GYUR,

00:04:03.573 --> 00:04:05.070
This is a tough verse,

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.857
although the words are not so difficult.

00:04:07.857 --> 00:04:10.200
CI STE LAS NI MA BYAS NA

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.280
If you could have karma
without anyone doing it

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.670
because you say karma has
to have its own nature

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.730
which implies that karma never changes,

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.163
which means that it didn't have

00:04:20.163 --> 00:04:22.213
anyone that did it. Got it?

00:04:22.213 --> 00:04:25.060
So if you say karma has a nature,

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.600
then natures don't change.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.574
Then okay, so someone, it cannot be anyone

00:04:31.574 --> 00:04:35.067
who committed the karma
if it's unchanging.

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:37.012
Got it?

00:04:37.012 --> 00:04:38.233
MA BYAS PA DANG PHRAD 'JIGS 'GYUR

00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:41.212
Then you get into the problem of...

00:04:41.212 --> 00:04:42.430
things could happen to you

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:46.780
without committing the karma before.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.140
Let's go through the logic again.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.360
He says, "Karma is self-existent",

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.670
meaning karma has its own nature.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:54.503
Okay.

00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:56.810
Nature, which we already
talked about in the chapter

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.079
"Investigation of Nature", or identity.

00:05:00.079 --> 00:05:03.295
It means that it doesn't change.

00:05:03.295 --> 00:05:05.500
Peripheral qualities change.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.110
The color of the fire changes.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.590
The fact that it's hot doesn't change.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.260
That's self-nature. That's an identity.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.660
It doesn't change.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.370
So if something doesn't change,

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.050
if karma has a self-identity,

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.480
it cannot change.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.610
No more than fire could become cold

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:21.701
and still be fire.

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:25.520
So therefore, no one did karma.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.995
Therefore, you can have karmic
results without someone doing them.

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:33.439
Therefore, things can happen
to you that you don't deserve.

00:05:33.439 --> 00:05:37.615
Got it? You okay? You following?

00:05:37.615 --> 00:05:41.630
If karma's unchanging,
then nobody did karma.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.540
But karma still works, so karma can work

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.350
without anybody doing it.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.133
Therefore, things can happen
to you that you didn't deserve

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.066
because you didn't do anything.

00:05:51.066 --> 00:05:52.040
Got it?

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.948
Then that's going to be a weird world.

00:05:54.948 --> 00:05:56.860
MA BYAS PA DANG PHRAD 'JIGS 'GYUR

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.523
MA BYAS PA is the third law of karma.

00:06:00.523 --> 00:06:02.380
If you don't do it, you
cannot get a result.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.350
And he says, "No, now you have to
change the third law of karma."

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.440
If karma is self-existent,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.970
then you could have karma running around

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.145
that no one committed.

00:06:11.145 --> 00:06:12.560
Karmic results could happen to you

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.542
for things you never did.

00:06:15.542 --> 00:06:19.958
Which is what you accuse the universe
constantly already. [laughter]

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:22.960
MA BYAS PA DANG PHRAD 'JIGS 'GYUR,

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.938
This 'JIGS is spelled with an S.

00:06:25.938 --> 00:06:29.640
So it doesn't mean destroy,
it means, like 'JIGS MED.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.790
You'd have to walk
around on eggshells. Why?

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:35.860
Things could happen to you
that you don't deserve.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.860
Then you should be nervous.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:40.870
In a world, where you
don't have to make karma

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:45.477
to get karma back, then
you better be careful.

00:06:45.477 --> 00:06:48.419
You better keep your eyes out.

00:06:48.419 --> 00:06:50.740
TSANGS SPYOD GNAS PA MA YIN PA'ANG

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.120
This is a weird example,

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.278
and maybe you got to think about

00:06:53.278 --> 00:06:54.678
why he chose this example.

00:06:54.678 --> 00:06:57.117
He says, "You could be a person

00:06:57.117 --> 00:07:00.347
who keeps sexual purity very well,

00:07:00.347 --> 00:07:05.342
and still you would have bad results."

00:07:05.342 --> 00:07:07.890
Like the karmic results
of sexual impurity,

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.980
one of them is air pollution, for example.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:15.267
So he says, "If you
could get karmic results

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:17.097
for things you never did,

00:07:17.097 --> 00:07:19.057
then you could be a good monk,

00:07:19.057 --> 00:07:22.267
and keep your morality, as far as sex,

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:25.650
and then still you would
live in a polluted country."

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.483
Okay?

00:07:26.483 --> 00:07:29.614
You could get undeserved

00:07:29.614 --> 00:07:31.362
karmic results.

00:07:31.362 --> 00:07:33.550
MA YIN PA'ANG, DE LA
SKYON DU THAL BAR 'GYUR

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:37.491
These are all the examples
of problems that would come

00:07:37.491 --> 00:07:40.850
from your idea that karma
has its own identity

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:44.942
in the same way that you thought
fire had it's own identity.

00:07:45.845 --> 00:07:48.508
Okay? Cool.

00:07:48.508 --> 00:07:49.341
All right.

00:07:49.341 --> 00:07:54.341
I have a picture of... that was
supposed to be air pollution

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.114
without cars, or something.

00:07:57.114 --> 00:07:58.016
I don't know.

00:07:58.016 --> 00:08:00.040
Pretend there is no cars.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.620
But it's still polluted.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.280
You got the results of sexual misconduct,

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:08.712
even though you were very
pure with your behavior.

00:08:08.712 --> 00:08:10.040
All right.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.290
Why he chose that one out of the ten.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.220
Maybe we all have this problem.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.068
Maybe we all have some kind of problem.

00:08:17.068 --> 00:08:20.351
All right, next verse.

00:08:20.351 --> 00:08:22.002
,THA SNYAD THAMS CAD NYID DANG YANG,

00:08:22.002 --> 00:08:25.455
,'GAL BAR 'GYUR BAR THE TSOM MED,

00:08:25.455 --> 00:08:26.888
THA SNYAD THAMS CAD

00:08:26.888 --> 00:08:29.870
THA SNYAD means expression,

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:31.480
and Choney Lama says,

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:35.630
"He's talking about how the world talks.

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:38.140
So sometimes in Buddhist books,

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.697
they will say, "Oh, come on look,

00:08:39.697 --> 00:08:43.439
even in normal conversation
people don't accept that."

00:08:43.439 --> 00:08:46.503
Even normal people in the
world wouldn't say that.

00:08:46.503 --> 00:08:48.427
So that here it's THA
SNYAD THAMS CAD NYID DANG

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:50.330
Even when people get together and talk,

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:54.610
who are not Buddhist, they weren't
trained, still 'GAL BAR 'GYUR,

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:57.630
it would be a contradiction.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:01.205
For example, here is the picture. Yay!

00:09:04.594 --> 00:09:08.490
It would be a contradiction
to have a field

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:13.460
full of lettuce, I
guess, my enemy, lettuce,

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:16.280
and there is nobody who planted it.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.113
You know?

00:09:17.113 --> 00:09:20.540
So even with a good result,

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.490
like suddenly 2,000 heads of lettuce

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.610
grew in your garden by themselves,

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.868
still people would talk.

00:09:29.868 --> 00:09:31.237
- What happened?

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:33.587
- I don't know. It just showed up.

00:09:33.587 --> 00:09:35.070
- Wow, that's weird.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:38.180
See, even people in the normal world

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.620
understand that it's weird to get a result

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.116
when you didn't do anything.

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:45.700
Like, I don't know,

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:50.542
suddenly your backyard
blooms with all kind

00:09:50.542 --> 00:09:53.056
of delicious vegetables,
if there were such a thing.

00:09:53.056 --> 00:09:56.618
BRTAG PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS
PA, in theoretical case.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.980
Then even in the normal world,

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:02.230
people would say something's
weird is going on.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.880
He didn't plant any vegetables,

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:06.215
and look, he got all these
vegetables. 'GAL BAR 'GYUR

00:10:06.215 --> 00:10:08.431
,BSOD NAMS DANG NI SDIG BYED PA'I,

00:10:08.431 --> 00:10:11.010
,RNAM PAR DBYE BA'ANG 'THAD MI 'GYUR,

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.958
If you could get suddenly karmic results

00:10:14.958 --> 00:10:17.120
without having done anything

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.690
because karma has its own nature,

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.900
then there would be no good
deeds and bad deeds, either.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.110
You can forget the distinction.

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:27.040
You can forget the division

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.920
between good deeds and bad deeds

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.753
because you just going to get
randomly whatever you get.

00:10:31.753 --> 00:10:33.610
So why talk about good
deeds and bad deeds?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.120
Good deeds and bad deeds,

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.190
morality in Buddhism is defined

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.890
by the karma that you get back.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:41.723
Okay?

00:10:41.723 --> 00:10:43.173
How do you decide right and wrong

00:10:43.173 --> 00:10:45.989
in a Buddhist world?

00:10:45.989 --> 00:10:47.270
Does it hurt when it comes back,

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:49.220
or does it make you
happy when it comes back?

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:51.387
That's right or wrong.

00:10:51.387 --> 00:10:52.830
That's the definition of right and wrong.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:56.063
It's not even that it hurts someone else.

00:10:56.063 --> 00:11:00.650
Ultimately, Buddhist
morality is based upon

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:03.190
will it hurt you if you do it?

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:06.490
And will it hurt you, will
it help you when you do it?

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:07.520
Okay?

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.659
By the way, always through
hurting someone else, right?

00:11:10.659 --> 00:11:13.177
All right, next one.

00:11:13.177 --> 00:11:15.700
Next verse.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.390
,DE NI RNAM SMIN SMIN 'GYUR PA,

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:19.710
By the way,

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.860
I disagree with

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.640
this line in Choney Lama.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.490
I think someone added it.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.290
The Tengyur says different.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.487
And Choney Lama's commentary says,

00:11:30.487 --> 00:11:32.770
"matches the Tengyur."

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:35.040
So I think someone added
the root text later,

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:39.430
and was adding a different version.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.772
It matters, okay?

00:11:41.772 --> 00:11:43.610
So I am going to change
this line to fit the Tengyur

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.690
because that matches Choney Lama.

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:48.185
So here it is,

00:11:48.185 --> 00:11:50.209
,DE NI RNAM SMIN SMIN 'GYUR PA,

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:53.527
,YANG DANG YANG DU RNAM SMIN 'GYUR,

00:11:53.527 --> 00:11:55.710
If karma could come back
to you when you didn't

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.180
do anything in the first place,

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.010
then when karma ripens on you,

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:02.034
that ripening could ripen again.

00:12:03.901 --> 00:12:08.100
If you could get a flat tire on your car

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:10.650
without hurting someone else's car,

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:15.618
then the flat tire would go flat, also.

00:12:15.618 --> 00:12:18.440
[laughing]

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.800
The karma would pile up on itself.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.603
If no one had to commit the
karma for you to get the result,

00:12:23.603 --> 00:12:25.890
then you could keep getting results.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.505
Not just one, but they
could repeat themselves.

00:12:29.505 --> 00:12:30.880
,GAL TE RANG BZHIN YOD NA NI,

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:34.943
,GANG PHYIR LAS GNAS DE YI PHYIR,

00:12:34.943 --> 00:12:36.268
Okay?

00:12:36.268 --> 00:12:38.570
And then another problem.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.278
And he kind of switches,

00:12:40.278 --> 00:12:41.852
he's been talking about the result,

00:12:41.852 --> 00:12:45.018
but now he talks about the karma itself.

00:12:46.827 --> 00:12:50.240
If karma could come back to
you without doing anything,

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.497
then when you did do something,

00:12:54.497 --> 00:12:56.380
that actually could go on forever,

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.894
and never produce a result.

00:12:59.894 --> 00:13:03.310
If karma came from its own side,

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:05.230
then when you did something,

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:08.963
it would be logical that that
action would continue forever.

00:13:08.963 --> 00:13:11.280
And it would never ripen

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:14.304
because the karma had its own
nature that doesn't change.

00:13:14.304 --> 00:13:16.430
Identity doesn't change.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:18.960
If the karma has an identity,

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.977
the definition of an identity
is that it doesn't change.

00:13:21.977 --> 00:13:23.630
It stays with you.

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:27.010
So therefore, if karma is action,

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:29.570
then you would always
be in a state of action,

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:32.538
and you would never get
a result from the karma.

00:13:32.538 --> 00:13:35.020
Then there would be no time
for the karma to come back

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.400
because you have to be
doing it all the time,

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.550
because it's not supposed to change,

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.289
because it has its own identity.

00:13:41.289 --> 00:13:43.020
And you do not change identity.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.900
Identity means something you
keep that doesn't change,

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:49.020
like heat with fire.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.860
I have a nice picture.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:54.020
I call this "Workaholic Karma".

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.470
And I think it would be
a nice name for a band.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:58.548
"Workaholic Karma".

00:13:58.548 --> 00:14:02.043
It means the karma keeps
working, and nothing happens.

00:14:02.043 --> 00:14:03.030
[laughing]

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:05.350
You keep killing people,
or you keep saving life,

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:07.600
or donating to Club de Oro,

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:09.555
and it never comes back to you.

00:14:09.555 --> 00:14:11.650
You just keep doing
it, doing it, doing it.

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:12.860
Because why?

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.450
Because karma can't change.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.550
- Why? - It has an identity of its own.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.383
- Why?

00:14:17.383 --> 00:14:19.622
- Because it's not coming from me.

00:14:19.622 --> 00:14:21.830
The laws of karma are not coming from me.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.648
All right.

00:14:23.648 --> 00:14:25.651
"Workaholic Karma"

00:14:25.651 --> 00:14:29.523
I think it's going to
be a good book title.

00:14:29.523 --> 00:14:31.267
Next verse.

00:14:31.267 --> 00:14:32.675
,LAS 'DI NYON MONGS DAG NYID LA,

00:14:32.675 --> 00:14:34.325
,NYON MONGS DE DAG YANG DAG MIN,

00:14:34.325 --> 00:14:36.091
,GAL TE NYON MONGS YANG DAG MIN,

00:14:36.091 --> 00:14:39.550
,LAS NI YANG DAG JI LTAR YIN,

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:41.402
The suffering of life,

00:14:41.402 --> 00:14:44.409
the truth of suffering,

00:14:44.409 --> 00:14:47.220
the first of the four higher truths,

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.600
arya truths, is suffering.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:53.717
What's a second higher truth?

00:14:53.717 --> 00:14:55.483
- [Student] Cause. - Is the cause.

00:14:55.483 --> 00:14:59.290
Which is traditionally
divided into two, for $100.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.850
The cause of all
suffering is traditionally

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:06.742
divided into two when you
teach the four truths.

00:15:06.742 --> 00:15:09.517
- [Student] Misunderstanding.

00:15:09.517 --> 00:15:12.554
- No.

00:15:12.554 --> 00:15:13.795
- Cancel the bet.

00:15:13.795 --> 00:15:16.434
LAS 'DI NYON MONGS.

00:15:16.434 --> 00:15:17.267
LAS

00:15:17.267 --> 00:15:18.100
- [Student] Karma and emotion.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:19.640
- Karma and negative emotions.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.465
You can call it mental afflictions,

00:15:22.465 --> 00:15:26.665
but that word hasn't been
used since the late 1700s,

00:15:26.665 --> 00:15:29.185
and Buddhist scholars.

00:15:29.185 --> 00:15:30.690
Okay.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:34.221
So anyway, let's call
it negative emotions.

00:15:34.221 --> 00:15:35.171
LAS 'DI NYON MONGS

00:15:35.171 --> 00:15:37.530
These are the two sources of suffering.

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:39.234
Here he says,

00:15:39.234 --> 00:15:42.482
LAS 'DI NYON MONGS DAG NYID LA

00:15:42.482 --> 00:15:44.948
Dirty karma,

00:15:44.948 --> 00:15:46.948
that the essence of dirty karma

00:15:46.948 --> 00:15:50.460
is negative emotions, isn't it?

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:55.002
Dirty karmas, dirty
karma, ZAG BCAS KYI LAS.

00:15:55.002 --> 00:15:56.567
The nature of dirty karma is that

00:15:56.567 --> 00:15:59.601
it is driven by your negative emotions.

00:15:59.601 --> 00:16:01.930
NYON MONGS DE DAG YANG DAG MIN

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:03.481
Those negative emotions are not

00:16:03.481 --> 00:16:06.057
YANG DAG, for $50.

00:16:06.057 --> 00:16:06.890
YANG DAG

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:07.973
- Huh? - [Student] Pure.

00:16:07.973 --> 00:16:10.440
- Yay! 50 dollars, give, by the way,

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:14.357
somebody won a 100 dollars
while you were gone.

00:16:15.856 --> 00:16:18.672
Okay.

00:16:18.672 --> 00:16:22.470
Pure. $100 for who can explain pure to me.

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.803
He says here,

00:16:23.803 --> 00:16:27.669
"Your negative emotions are not pure."

00:16:27.669 --> 00:16:31.955
[someone talking indistinctly]

00:16:36.888 --> 00:16:38.263
I mean, does Nagarjuna,

00:16:38.263 --> 00:16:42.030
does Arya Nagarjuna
really have to tell you

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:44.750
that your jealousy and anger are not nice.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.486
Is that what he's doing?

00:16:47.486 --> 00:16:49.605
Would he bother to tell you that?

00:16:49.605 --> 00:16:50.688
- [Student] Pain and [unclear].

00:16:50.688 --> 00:16:53.563
- Yay! $100 for Rebecca.

00:16:53.563 --> 00:16:56.980
This pure means exists
from their own side.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:59.407
Because obviously,
Nagarjuna is going to say,

00:16:59.407 --> 00:17:01.530
"Hey, guess what? Your
jealousy is a bad thing."

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.854
- Wow, I didn't know.

00:17:03.854 --> 00:17:05.730
[laughing]

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.280
So it's not pure.

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.490
GAL TE NYON MONGS YANG DAG MIN

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.770
If your negative emotions are impure,

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:18.581
then how can karma be pure?

00:17:18.581 --> 00:17:20.110
- [Student] It can't.

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:24.220
- Because your negative
emotions drive your..

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.750
- [Student] Actions.
- Karma.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.960
If the negative emotions are not pure,

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.970
meaning not coming from their own side,

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:34.221
then what they drive can be...

00:17:34.221 --> 00:17:35.600
coming from its own side.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:36.433
Got it?

00:17:36.433 --> 00:17:38.930
And that's the last
verse, he just finished.

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:40.780
If they were unchanging, they'd be coming,

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.913
if they were coming from their own
side, they would be unchanging.

00:17:42.913 --> 00:17:44.420
If they're unchanging,
you could get results

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.912
that you don't deserve.

00:17:46.912 --> 00:17:48.610
Got it?

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:51.280
Therefore, I could prove
it to you another way.

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:54.010
- Look, karma doesn't
exist for its own side.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:54.900
- Why?

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:58.610
It's made by things that don't
exist from their own side.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:17:59.747
Got it?

00:17:59.747 --> 00:18:02.217
If something makes another thing,

00:18:02.217 --> 00:18:03.880
and it doesn't come from its own side,

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.510
then the thing that the thing makes

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:06.343
shouldn't come from its own side, either.

00:18:06.343 --> 00:18:07.709
Got it?

00:18:07.709 --> 00:18:09.660
Therefore, karma doesn't
come from its own side.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:13.293
I just proved it to you a different way.

00:18:13.293 --> 00:18:16.140
I have an apple rotten, apple rotten,

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.120
rotten apple.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.688
I was thinking of Johnny Rotten Pizza.

00:18:19.688 --> 00:18:20.830
Ha-ha.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:22.296
Anyway,

00:18:23.371 --> 00:18:24.970
if the apple's rotten, then the apple pie

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.189
you make from the apple is going to be...

00:18:27.189 --> 00:18:29.772
- [Student] Rotten.
- Rotten.

00:18:29.772 --> 00:18:32.113
Why am I talking about that?

00:18:32.955 --> 00:18:35.730
- [Student] Then karma...

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:37.790
- What's the rotten apple?

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:39.820
- [Student] Negative emotions.
- Negative emotions.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.289
- What's the pie?

00:18:41.289 --> 00:18:43.520
- [Student] Karma.
- Karma, good.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:46.610
If you use rotten apples
to make an apple pie,

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:49.480
then the apple pie is
going to taste rotten.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.407
If you use

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:57.915
un-self-existent jealousy to create karma,

00:18:57.915 --> 00:18:59.330
then the karma that's made from

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:01.088
the un-self-existent jealousy

00:19:01.088 --> 00:19:04.138
is going to be un-self-existent.

00:19:04.138 --> 00:19:07.105
Rotten and rotten, got it?

00:19:07.105 --> 00:19:09.030
All right, just for fun,

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:13.055
we're going to do a Sanskrit
word called kleśa (klesha).

00:19:13.055 --> 00:19:16.680
And I don't know, it's
a big theme right here.

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:18.933
Negative emotions.

00:19:18.933 --> 00:19:20.670
So most of you know this word already.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:23.127
But I had to put something.

00:19:24.027 --> 00:19:29.001
Klesha means a negative emotion.

00:19:29.001 --> 00:19:30.567
It comes from the word √kliś

00:19:30.567 --> 00:19:32.417
which means to be bothered,

00:19:32.417 --> 00:19:35.404
or irritated, or distressed.

00:19:35.404 --> 00:19:40.320
And the English cognate is
"holly" because it's prickly.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.030
So when you talk about negative emotions

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.371
in Buddhism, RANG RGYUD LDAN
GYI GANG ZAG GI SHES RGYUD

00:19:46.371 --> 00:19:47.777
MA ZHI BAR BYED PA'I SEMS BYUNG SEMS PA

00:19:47.777 --> 00:19:51.863
Say RANG RGYUD LDAN GYI

00:19:51.863 --> 00:19:56.797
GANG ZAG GI SHES RGYUD
MA ZHI BAR BYED PA'I

00:19:57.797 --> 00:20:00.314
SEMS BYUNG SEMS PA

00:20:00.314 --> 00:20:01.400
A state of mind which ruins

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.500
the peace of mind of
the person who has it.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:05.910
A state of mind which ruins

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.750
the peace of mind of
the person who has it.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:12.120
Definition of a klesha, negative emotion.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:14.269
And it's prickly.

00:20:14.269 --> 00:20:15.653
That's the point.

00:20:15.653 --> 00:20:18.730
It disturbs your peace of
mind because it's prickly.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:20.210
Jealousy is prickly.

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.630
And when you keep jealousy in your heart,

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.860
then you can't really be jolly all day.

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.690
So you've always got
something bothering you.

00:20:28.573 --> 00:20:31.127
Jolly all day is a great spiritual goal.

00:20:32.152 --> 00:20:33.484
All right.

00:20:35.093 --> 00:20:36.881
Next verse.

00:20:36.881 --> 00:20:37.956
,LAS DANG NYON MONGS PA DAG NI,

00:20:37.956 --> 00:20:40.248
,LUS RNAMS KYI NI RKYEN DU BSTAN,

00:20:40.248 --> 00:20:42.638
,GAL TE LAS DANG NYON MONGS PA,

00:20:42.638 --> 00:20:46.971
,DE STONG LUS LA JI LTAR BRJOD,

00:20:46.971 --> 00:20:48.533
LAS DANG NYON MONGS PA DAG NI

00:20:48.533 --> 00:20:50.560
These two things that
we've been talking about,

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:54.156
karma and negative emotions,

00:20:54.156 --> 00:20:55.912
LUS RNAMS KYI NI RKYEN DU BSTAN

00:20:55.912 --> 00:20:59.810
they were taught by the Buddha

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:03.543
to be the RKYEN of your LUS.

00:21:03.543 --> 00:21:07.891
To be the cause of your mortal coil.

00:21:07.891 --> 00:21:11.641
This is a English special
expression, mortal coil.

00:21:13.623 --> 00:21:16.170
Yes, the body, the dying body

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.780
that you are wearing right now.

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:19.810
It's called mortal coil.

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:20.643
I don't know why coil.

00:21:20.643 --> 00:21:23.729
It wraps around you, or something.

00:21:23.729 --> 00:21:26.420
Anyway, this clothing called your body,

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:30.081
which will be dropped,

00:21:30.081 --> 00:21:31.856
it's caused by two factors,

00:21:31.856 --> 00:21:34.997
karma and negative emotions.

00:21:34.997 --> 00:21:36.939
GAL TE LAS DANG NYON MONGS PA

00:21:36.939 --> 00:21:38.770
DE STONG

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.061
If the karma and negative emotions

00:21:41.061 --> 00:21:44.028
which creates your body are STONG,

00:21:44.028 --> 00:21:46.483
"empty", then LUS LA JI LTAR BRJOD

00:21:46.483 --> 00:21:48.300
Then what? Duh.

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:51.279
What do you think the body will be?

00:21:51.279 --> 00:21:53.550
JI LTAR BRJOD

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:55.313
What did you think the body?

00:21:55.313 --> 00:21:57.170
Did you think it's not going to be empty?

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:00.960
If the body is made by
two super-empty things,

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:04.860
then the body's also super-empty.

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:07.530
That's Nagarjuna.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:10.670
I have a picture of a skyscraper

00:22:10.670 --> 00:22:12.770
made with bubbles.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:15.340
It was midnight, I was getting silly.

00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:18.798
I don't quite remember why.

00:22:18.798 --> 00:22:21.786
I mean...

00:22:21.786 --> 00:22:23.580
if the things that are

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:26.500
the foundations of an entity are impure,

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:28.410
then the entity is
going to be impure also.

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:32.510
And it probably won't stand very well.

00:22:32.510 --> 00:22:35.355
Next one.

00:22:37.497 --> 00:22:41.000
In these next three verses,

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:43.530
the other guy gets to come back

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:46.526
and insist that he's right.

00:22:48.509 --> 00:22:49.383
Here we go.

00:22:49.383 --> 00:22:52.440
Karma must exist from its own side.

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:54.465
All right.

00:22:54.465 --> 00:22:56.701
And now, specifically,

00:22:56.701 --> 00:22:59.180
the other guy's going
to talk about the person

00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:01.240
who commits the karma.

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:02.715
He wants to prove,

00:23:02.715 --> 00:23:06.970
he's done trying to prove that
the karma has its own nature.

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:10.470
He wants to prove that
the person who commits

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.745
the karma has their own nature.

00:23:12.745 --> 00:23:16.207
He kind of gave up on, okay Nargarjuna,

00:23:16.207 --> 00:23:19.481
suppose the karma doesn't
have its own nature.

00:23:19.481 --> 00:23:22.160
And therefore, the body,

00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:24.468
it's not true that the body
doesn't have its own nature

00:23:24.468 --> 00:23:25.600
because the thing that made the body

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:26.629
didn't have its own nature.

00:23:26.629 --> 00:23:28.520
Let's give up on that.

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:31.186
Let's just talk about the
guy who committed the karma:

00:23:31.186 --> 00:23:32.880
good karma or bad karma.

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:34.870
Do they have a nature of their own?

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:37.461
Well, listen, Nagarjuna,

00:23:37.461 --> 00:23:40.386
,MA RIG BSGRIBS PA'I SKYE BO GANG,

00:23:40.386 --> 00:23:43.050
You got a person, SKYE BO,

00:23:43.050 --> 00:23:46.120
who's blinded, BSGRIBS PA,

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:48.274
by MA RIG PA.

00:23:48.274 --> 00:23:50.178
Misunderstanding.

00:23:50.178 --> 00:23:52.710
So the other guy's
showing he's a Buddhist.

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:55.392
Maybe he's Abhidharma or something.

00:23:55.392 --> 00:23:58.210
Look, come on, let's talk
about normal sansara.

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:02.500
You got a person who has blinded by,

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.390
they don't understand anything.

00:24:04.390 --> 00:24:07.182
Let's go back to the verse.

00:24:07.182 --> 00:24:09.520
,SRED LDAN DE MI ZA BA PO,

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:11.520
That person who has SRED PA,

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:12.590
meaning desire.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:15.160
It doesn't mean you like sex.

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:17.740
It means you attach to thinking things

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:19.420
come from their own side.

00:24:19.420 --> 00:24:22.010
Which means you can
also get anger from it,

00:24:22.010 --> 00:24:23.800
with your husband, for example.

00:24:23.800 --> 00:24:27.042
If you think he's coming
from his own side.

00:24:27.042 --> 00:24:28.856
And then comes this beautiful word,

00:24:28.856 --> 00:24:31.450
ZA BA PO

00:24:31.450 --> 00:24:33.660
ZA BA means to eat dinner.

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:35.520
What's a ZA BA PO?

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:37.245
Yeah.

00:24:37.245 --> 00:24:40.173
But what's the dinner?

00:24:40.173 --> 00:24:42.164
[someone speaking indistinctly]

00:24:42.164 --> 00:24:46.264
We're talking about someone
who commits a karma.

00:24:46.264 --> 00:24:48.780
- [Student] It's a result of that.

00:24:48.780 --> 00:24:51.215
- What? Why refer to the person who

00:24:51.215 --> 00:24:53.230
commits a karma as the eater?

00:24:53.230 --> 00:24:55.800
Why should we call the consumer?

00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.600
The eater.

00:24:57.600 --> 00:24:59.020
[someone speaking indistinctly]

00:24:59.020 --> 00:25:01.870
Yeah, then he's going to eat the result.

00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:03.430
Perfect.

00:25:03.430 --> 00:25:06.477
The person who commits the karma

00:25:06.477 --> 00:25:11.218
will become the consumer of
the result of that karma.

00:25:11.218 --> 00:25:13.237
You're going to have, what do you call it?

00:25:13.237 --> 00:25:14.978
You eat your cake, or...

00:25:14.978 --> 00:25:15.909
- [Student] Have your
cake and eat it, too.

00:25:15.909 --> 00:25:17.680
- No, there's another one.

00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:22.680
You're going to have to
eat the meal you cooked.

00:25:22.942 --> 00:25:26.027
- [Student] Make your bed and lie in it.

00:25:26.027 --> 00:25:29.670
- Yeah, you made your bed and now
you're going to have to lie in it.

00:25:29.670 --> 00:25:31.940
You hurt somebody,

00:25:31.940 --> 00:25:35.076
two weeks later you're
going to be the ZA BA PO.

00:25:35.076 --> 00:25:36.701
You're going to eat that karma,

00:25:36.701 --> 00:25:40.176
it's going to come back to you.

00:25:40.176 --> 00:25:43.309
$100: can you guess what
the discussion is here?

00:25:43.309 --> 00:25:45.020
I'll say it again.

00:25:45.020 --> 00:25:48.836
You did a karma, the karma stayed as..

00:25:48.836 --> 00:25:51.686
"don't lose it".

00:25:51.686 --> 00:25:54.792
And then it came back to you.

00:25:54.792 --> 00:25:56.020
What's the question going to be here?

00:25:56.020 --> 00:25:59.338
What's the Nagarjuna's

00:25:59.338 --> 00:26:01.195
question he would bring up, Tim?

00:26:01.195 --> 00:26:02.560
- [Tim] Person would have to be a....

00:26:02.560 --> 00:26:04.990
- Yes, perfect, perfect.

00:26:04.990 --> 00:26:08.307
Hundred dollars for that young man.

00:26:09.974 --> 00:26:14.110
We're interested in
what happened to the guy

00:26:14.110 --> 00:26:15.630
who made the karma.

00:26:15.630 --> 00:26:19.076
And what's his relation to the...?

00:26:19.076 --> 00:26:20.007
Eater.

00:26:20.007 --> 00:26:22.823
Yes, to the consumer.

00:26:22.823 --> 00:26:23.656
He makes the pie,

00:26:23.656 --> 00:26:25.822
two weeks later another guy eats the pie.

00:26:25.822 --> 00:26:27.150
What's their relationship?

00:26:27.150 --> 00:26:28.720
Is he still that guy?

00:26:28.720 --> 00:26:30.730
And that doesn't make sense.

00:26:30.730 --> 00:26:31.870
Right?

00:26:31.870 --> 00:26:32.930
Good answer.

00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:35.723
You're already thinking like Nagarjuna.

00:26:35.723 --> 00:26:37.889
,SRED LDAN DE MI ZA BA PO,

00:26:37.889 --> 00:26:41.031
,DE YANG BYED LAS GZHAN MIN ZHING,

00:26:41.031 --> 00:26:43.788
Are they someone different from the

00:26:43.788 --> 00:26:44.621
BYED?

00:26:44.621 --> 00:26:46.830
Here BYED means 'doer'.

00:26:46.830 --> 00:26:48.768
It doesn't mean to do.

00:26:48.768 --> 00:26:50.040
BYED PA PO

00:26:50.040 --> 00:26:51.840
Unfortunately we're in poetry,

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:54.957
and we got to cut the words short.

00:26:54.957 --> 00:26:57.073
Then, Nagarjuna says,

00:26:57.073 --> 00:27:00.340
BYED PA PO LAS GZHAN MIN

00:27:00.340 --> 00:27:03.400
The guy who eats the result of the action

00:27:03.400 --> 00:27:07.096
two weeks later he is not GZHAN.

00:27:07.096 --> 00:27:10.387
Yeah, he's not a different
guy, he's the same guy.

00:27:10.387 --> 00:27:12.020
What?
[laughing]

00:27:12.020 --> 00:27:14.962
He's the same guy,

00:27:14.962 --> 00:27:17.650
,DE NYID DE YANG MA YIN NO,

00:27:17.650 --> 00:27:21.542
By the way, this is the other guy talking.

00:27:21.542 --> 00:27:23.360
I'm sorry, I should of said that.

00:27:23.360 --> 00:27:25.690
It's the same guy who eats the karma,

00:27:25.690 --> 00:27:27.740
who did the karma two weeks ago.

00:27:27.740 --> 00:27:29.020
That's the same guy.

00:27:29.020 --> 00:27:29.853
But in another way,

00:27:29.853 --> 00:27:31.708
DE NYID DE YANG MA YIN

00:27:31.708 --> 00:27:32.541
When you think about it,

00:27:32.541 --> 00:27:35.499
it's not really the same guy, either.

00:27:35.499 --> 00:27:38.406
So it seems like the
debater, the other debater?

00:27:38.406 --> 00:27:39.320
He's waffling.

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:40.590
He says, "Come on, it's the same guy."

00:27:40.590 --> 00:27:41.948
And he says, "But in a way,

00:27:41.948 --> 00:27:44.756
he's not the same guy, is he?"

00:27:44.756 --> 00:27:48.211
So he's waffling.

00:27:48.211 --> 00:27:49.310
Then here is our reply.

00:27:49.310 --> 00:27:53.143
Nagarjuna comes to the rescue.

00:27:53.143 --> 00:27:54.406
,GANG GI PHYIR NA LAS 'DI NI,

00:27:54.406 --> 00:27:57.631
,RKYEN LAS BYUNG BA MA YIN ZHING,

00:27:58.614 --> 00:28:01.700
If karma existed from its own side,

00:28:01.700 --> 00:28:05.676
it could never come from a cause.

00:28:05.676 --> 00:28:08.838
If karma existed from its own side,

00:28:08.838 --> 00:28:11.070
that would be its identity.

00:28:11.070 --> 00:28:15.756
And it could not be
triggered by some action.

00:28:15.756 --> 00:28:19.480
,RKYEN MIN LAS BYUNG YOD MIN PA,

00:28:19.480 --> 00:28:22.410
If you had a karma that happened

00:28:22.410 --> 00:28:24.160
without anybody doing anything,

00:28:24.160 --> 00:28:27.752
well that would be a non-existent karma.

00:28:28.685 --> 00:28:30.040
,DE PHYIR BYED PA PO YANG MED,

00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:32.570
And therefore, since there was no karma,

00:28:32.570 --> 00:28:35.587
which was done by anything,
there's nobody who did it.

00:28:35.587 --> 00:28:37.690
So why you worried about
whether he's the same

00:28:37.690 --> 00:28:38.910
as the other later guy?

00:28:38.910 --> 00:28:40.870
Because there is no guy who did it.

00:28:40.870 --> 00:28:41.703
Because he's not possible,

00:28:41.703 --> 00:28:44.450
because usually karma
comes from its own side.

00:28:44.450 --> 00:28:48.008
Nagarjuna is really kicking his ass.

00:28:48.008 --> 00:28:49.050
I'll say it again.

00:28:49.050 --> 00:28:50.960
Okay, yes, karma comes from its own side,

00:28:50.960 --> 00:28:52.256
and the eater comes from his own side.

00:28:52.256 --> 00:28:53.733
Why are you worried about it?

00:28:53.733 --> 00:28:55.631
If karma comes from its own side,

00:28:55.631 --> 00:28:56.464
then the eater comes from its own side,

00:28:56.464 --> 00:28:58.114
then the karma comes from its own side.

00:28:58.114 --> 00:28:59.040
The karma comes from its own side,

00:28:59.040 --> 00:29:00.360
doesn't have to have a cause.

00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:01.710
So nothing's going to happen.

00:29:01.710 --> 00:29:03.130
No one's going to do anything.

00:29:03.130 --> 00:29:04.800
Why you worried about
the guy who comes later,

00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:08.383
if the guy who comes
earlier wasn't there anyway?

00:29:08.383 --> 00:29:10.916
Got it?

00:29:10.916 --> 00:29:12.650
,GAL TE LAS DANG BYED MED NA,

00:29:12.650 --> 00:29:15.608
If there's no action done by nobody,

00:29:15.608 --> 00:29:16.441
Got it?

00:29:16.441 --> 00:29:19.470
If there's no action done by,

00:29:19.470 --> 00:29:24.442
if no action is done by nobody,

00:29:24.442 --> 00:29:25.920
,LAS SKYES 'BRAS BU GA LA YOD,

00:29:25.920 --> 00:29:26.800
Then how the [mimes expletive]

00:29:26.800 --> 00:29:29.583
are you going to have a karmic result?

00:29:29.583 --> 00:29:32.340
If there's no action done,

00:29:32.340 --> 00:29:34.760
if a non-action is done by a non-body,

00:29:34.760 --> 00:29:36.867
then what the hell is the result?

00:29:36.867 --> 00:29:39.170
GA LA YOD means what the hell.

00:29:39.170 --> 00:29:41.880
It's going to be a non-result.

00:29:41.880 --> 00:29:44.490
If a non-action is done by a non-body,

00:29:44.490 --> 00:29:46.740
then the non-body's non-action

00:29:46.740 --> 00:29:49.320
is going to have a none-result.

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:51.486
Got it?

00:29:51.486 --> 00:29:52.650
,CI STE 'BRAS BU YOD MIN NA,

00:29:52.650 --> 00:29:54.160
And if there's no result,

00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:57.226
why are you so worried about the ZA BA PO?

00:29:58.130 --> 00:29:59.855
Yeah. Why are you worried about the guy

00:29:59.855 --> 00:30:01.830
who's going to eat the result of the karma

00:30:01.830 --> 00:30:04.938
if there's no karma to eat.

00:30:04.938 --> 00:30:05.830
Got it?

00:30:05.830 --> 00:30:07.758
According to you.

00:30:07.758 --> 00:30:10.394
It's getting hot in here.

00:30:10.394 --> 00:30:11.352
All right.

00:30:11.352 --> 00:30:13.840
I want to have, look at this next picture.

00:30:13.840 --> 00:30:18.688
Now, this is amazing.

00:30:18.688 --> 00:30:22.230
This is what I want the
Peachtree Cafe to look like.

00:30:22.230 --> 00:30:26.033
Whether it will ever
happen, only God knows.

00:30:26.033 --> 00:30:28.736
But anyway,

00:30:28.736 --> 00:30:30.760
the distinctive feature of this picture is

00:30:30.760 --> 00:30:33.710
how many ZA BA POs in this picture?

00:30:33.710 --> 00:30:35.705
Nobody.

00:30:35.705 --> 00:30:38.073
There's nobody here eating.

00:30:38.073 --> 00:30:39.506
If a non-existent karma can be

00:30:39.506 --> 00:30:41.664
done by a non-existent guy,

00:30:41.664 --> 00:30:43.720
why the hell are you
worried about the eater?

00:30:43.720 --> 00:30:44.850
There is no eater.

00:30:44.850 --> 00:30:47.460
And I showed you a picture with no eater.

00:30:47.460 --> 00:30:48.720
I hope there will be eaters,

00:30:48.720 --> 00:30:51.140
but this one has no eaters.

00:30:51.140 --> 00:30:54.733
All right, next verse.

00:30:54.733 --> 00:30:59.060
Three long, oh my gosh, three verses.

00:30:59.060 --> 00:31:03.026
The other guy says,

00:31:03.026 --> 00:31:07.007
"If you say karma has no identity at all,

00:31:07.007 --> 00:31:09.093
"you are SKUR BA 'DEBS PA-ed,

00:31:09.093 --> 00:31:10.651
the Buddhist teaching.

00:31:10.651 --> 00:31:12.984
SKUR 'DEBS and SGRO 'DOGS,
we had it yesterday,

00:31:12.984 --> 00:31:15.495
somebody won some money.

00:31:15.495 --> 00:31:19.850
You are saying something which
does exist doesn't exist.

00:31:19.850 --> 00:31:21.530
So the guy comes back.

00:31:21.530 --> 00:31:23.846
If there's no eater and
there's nothing to eat,

00:31:23.846 --> 00:31:26.788
and nobody made their food to eat,

00:31:26.788 --> 00:31:29.430
you are goddamn not
following Buddhist teaching.

00:31:29.430 --> 00:31:32.418
You are disrespecting Buddha.

00:31:32.418 --> 00:31:35.261
Who's that? The other guy.

00:31:35.261 --> 00:31:37.736
Now here's our... here we go.

00:31:37.736 --> 00:31:39.810
JI LTAR STON PAS SPRUL

00:31:39.810 --> 00:31:40.835
Here's our answer,

00:31:40.835 --> 00:31:43.868
and it's the last part of this,

00:31:43.868 --> 00:31:48.633
this is the end of the
classes, the end of the course.

00:31:48.633 --> 00:31:50.690
Except we will have a
review in the next class.

00:31:50.690 --> 00:31:52.723
There will be another class.

00:31:52.723 --> 00:31:55.580
But, here's the ultimate answer

00:31:55.580 --> 00:31:58.180
from the whole 15 classes.

00:31:58.180 --> 00:32:01.640
Here's the ultimate
answer to the accusation

00:32:01.640 --> 00:32:04.229
that we are disrespecting the Buddha

00:32:04.229 --> 00:32:06.110
because we say nobody eats the karma.

00:32:06.110 --> 00:32:07.430
Got it?

00:32:07.430 --> 00:32:10.806
Then we say, calm down, calm down.

00:32:10.806 --> 00:32:12.900
JI LTAR STON PAS SPRUL PA NI

00:32:12.900 --> 00:32:16.041
Listen, can the Buddha emanate or not?

00:32:16.041 --> 00:32:18.749
- [Student] Yes.

00:32:18.749 --> 00:32:19.830
- Yeah.

00:32:19.830 --> 00:32:22.460
By the way, it's two classical emanations:

00:32:22.460 --> 00:32:25.027
living and non-living.

00:32:25.027 --> 00:32:27.944
What's that mean?

00:32:28.800 --> 00:32:32.887
I mean, Buddha can emanate as a fish,

00:32:32.887 --> 00:32:33.720
or as a bridge.

00:32:33.720 --> 00:32:36.603
The famous example is a bridge,

00:32:36.603 --> 00:32:37.610
or a tree,

00:32:37.610 --> 00:32:39.500
or the ocean waves to teach you

00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:43.261
when you're sitting at
the beach next week.

00:32:44.328 --> 00:32:47.798
So can the Buddha

00:32:47.798 --> 00:32:50.890
show emanations

00:32:50.890 --> 00:32:55.657
that are kind of, how do you say?

00:32:55.657 --> 00:32:57.740
They're almost unreal in a way.

00:32:57.740 --> 00:32:59.863
Is that tree real?

00:32:59.863 --> 00:33:02.846
When the Buddha emanates as a tree,

00:33:02.846 --> 00:33:04.080
is it a real tree?

00:33:04.080 --> 00:33:05.830
If you climb the tree,

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:08.497
what are you really climbing?

00:33:08.497 --> 00:33:10.910
You're climbing Lord Buddha, okay?

00:33:10.910 --> 00:33:13.110
- Can Buddha emanate as a tree?

00:33:13.110 --> 00:33:14.200
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, we all read

00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:16.120
that Buddha can emanate as a tree.

00:33:16.120 --> 00:33:17.660
- So when you climb that tree,

00:33:17.660 --> 00:33:20.690
you're really climbing up
the Buddha's nose and stuff.

00:33:20.690 --> 00:33:21.617
- No, no, no, no, no.

00:33:21.617 --> 00:33:23.720
It's just kind of an illusion.

00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:28.720
The real Buddha is up in the
heaven, LONGS SPRUL, Tushita heaven.

00:33:28.730 --> 00:33:31.440
He's just emanating a tree.

00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:33.090
I'm not like disrespecting the Buddha

00:33:33.090 --> 00:33:35.610
when I climb on a tree
that the Buddha's emanating

00:33:35.610 --> 00:33:37.161
because that's not really the Buddha,

00:33:37.161 --> 00:33:38.730
it's just an emanation of the Buddha.

00:33:38.730 --> 00:33:40.197
And then, the Nagarjuna says,

00:33:40.197 --> 00:33:43.147
"Okay, I'm cool with that".

00:33:43.147 --> 00:33:45.010
JI LTAR STON PAS SPRUL PA NI

00:33:45.010 --> 00:33:46.890
Now I have a question for you.

00:33:46.890 --> 00:33:50.765
Could the tree put forth an emanation?

00:33:51.623 --> 00:33:53.223
Could Buddha, as a tree,

00:33:53.223 --> 00:33:56.197
could Buddha emanated as a tree

00:33:56.197 --> 00:33:58.989
emanate as an apple on the tree?

00:33:58.989 --> 00:34:00.389
- [Student] Sure, yes.

00:34:00.389 --> 00:34:03.730
- 10 minutes later, 10 minutes later.

00:34:03.730 --> 00:34:05.796
- Huh?

00:34:05.796 --> 00:34:06.629
Come on, listen,

00:34:06.629 --> 00:34:11.154
Listen, Buddha's emanating as
an apple tree in your backyard.

00:34:12.077 --> 00:34:14.259
I know.

00:34:14.259 --> 00:34:16.250
Would he or would he not have the power

00:34:16.250 --> 00:34:17.083
from that emanated tree

00:34:17.083 --> 00:34:19.216
to emanate an apple?

00:34:19.216 --> 00:34:21.130
- [Student] Yes.
- Of course, yes.

00:34:21.130 --> 00:34:23.940
That's what he's talking about here.

00:34:23.940 --> 00:34:28.918
And could he emanate a worm

00:34:28.918 --> 00:34:29.751
sitting on the apple

00:34:29.751 --> 00:34:31.484
on the tree that he emanated.

00:34:31.484 --> 00:34:32.490
- [Student] Yes.

00:34:32.490 --> 00:34:35.672
- Could the emanation have an emanation,

00:34:35.672 --> 00:34:36.892
and that emanation has another emanation?

00:34:36.892 --> 00:34:37.725
- [Student] Yes.

00:34:37.725 --> 00:34:38.680
- Yes, good.

00:34:38.680 --> 00:34:40.585
You're comfortable with that.

00:34:40.585 --> 00:34:41.940
,SLAR YANG GZHAN NI SPRUL PA LTAR,

00:34:41.940 --> 00:34:42.773
SLAR YANG GZHAN NI means

00:34:42.773 --> 00:34:44.773
he sends out a third emanation.

00:34:44.773 --> 00:34:46.680
Could the emanated tree emanate an apple?

00:34:46.680 --> 00:34:47.590
Yes.

00:34:47.590 --> 00:34:49.670
Could the emanated tree emanate an apple,

00:34:49.670 --> 00:34:50.780
emanate a worm?

00:34:50.780 --> 00:34:52.190
Yes.

00:34:52.190 --> 00:34:55.637
So what do you got the problem with karma?

00:34:56.962 --> 00:34:59.000
What's your problem?

00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:02.017
It's the same.

00:35:02.017 --> 00:35:05.190
You do something. It creates a seed.

00:35:05.190 --> 00:35:07.000
And that creates a result.

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:10.430
You are emanating a seed,

00:35:10.430 --> 00:35:12.610
and then the seed emanates a result,

00:35:12.610 --> 00:35:15.040
and the result kicks you in the ass.

00:35:15.040 --> 00:35:17.040
What's your problem?

00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:18.339
Why do you have a problem with that?

00:35:18.339 --> 00:35:21.770
He says, "Well, it's kind of similar."

00:35:21.770 --> 00:35:24.693
Is it real?

00:35:25.540 --> 00:35:28.510
That's the Nargarjuna. Is it real?

00:35:28.510 --> 00:35:32.333
Does it have to be real?

00:35:32.333 --> 00:35:35.521
Then his own answer is,

00:35:36.588 --> 00:35:38.788
,NYON MONGS LAS DANG LUS RNAMS DANG,

00:35:38.788 --> 00:35:40.260
,BYED PA PO DANG 'BRAS BU DAG,

00:35:40.260 --> 00:35:43.401
When you talk about karma
and mental afflictions

00:35:43.401 --> 00:35:44.830
creating a body,

00:35:44.830 --> 00:35:47.238
when you talk about an action

00:35:47.238 --> 00:35:49.845
creating a karmic result,

00:35:49.845 --> 00:35:53.195
it's all like the city of the Gandharvas.

00:35:54.988 --> 00:35:56.388
What's a city of the Gandharvas?

00:35:56.388 --> 00:35:58.766
The city,

00:35:58.766 --> 00:36:00.026
like, not Mexico City,

00:36:00.026 --> 00:36:00.859
Gandharva Mexico City.

00:36:00.859 --> 00:36:02.940
What's it mean? What's it mean?

00:36:02.940 --> 00:36:05.366
There's two kinds of gandharvas.

00:36:05.366 --> 00:36:06.199
- [Student] Celestial musicians.

00:36:06.199 --> 00:36:09.457
- One is the celestial
musicians who are cool guys.

00:36:09.457 --> 00:36:13.616
But the other is DRI ZA

00:36:13.616 --> 00:36:16.515
Gandha means sсent.

00:36:17.570 --> 00:36:20.903
- Yeah, smell eater, ghost, preta.

00:36:20.903 --> 00:36:22.850
Pretas are also called gandharvas.

00:36:22.850 --> 00:36:25.634
The city of the pretas...

00:36:25.634 --> 00:36:28.440
If you're a preta, and you
see a city on the horizon,

00:36:28.440 --> 00:36:30.630
and it's got fountains and apple trees,

00:36:30.630 --> 00:36:31.463
and all that kind of stuff,.

00:36:31.463 --> 00:36:33.347
And then you run towards it,

00:36:33.347 --> 00:36:36.030
and then suddenly it disappears.

00:36:36.030 --> 00:36:37.660
It's like a SMIG RGYU RMI LAM.

00:36:37.660 --> 00:36:39.830
Last two words of this beautiful chapter.

00:36:39.830 --> 00:36:42.720
The last two words of
this beautiful chapter.

00:36:42.720 --> 00:36:44.270
It's like an illusion.

00:36:44.270 --> 00:36:47.813
It's like a RMI LAM.

00:36:47.813 --> 00:36:50.491
It's like a dream.

00:36:50.491 --> 00:36:52.010
Yes, the karmic results that

00:36:52.010 --> 00:36:56.611
you are experiencing are like a dream.

00:36:56.611 --> 00:36:59.410
The sustaining of that karmic energy

00:36:59.410 --> 00:37:02.985
until the result comes back
to you is like a dream.

00:37:02.985 --> 00:37:06.743
The action in the first
place was like a dream.

00:37:06.743 --> 00:37:07.576
It's like an apple tree

00:37:07.576 --> 00:37:09.976
emanated by the Buddha,

00:37:09.976 --> 00:37:12.950
a fake apple tree giving fake fruits,

00:37:12.950 --> 00:37:16.641
and fake worms sitting on
the fruit. It's the same.

00:37:16.641 --> 00:37:19.850
It's the same. It's an illusion.

00:37:19.850 --> 00:37:21.260
Why is it an illusion?

00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:23.410
It looks like it's
coming from its own side,

00:37:23.410 --> 00:37:25.130
but it's not. It's coming from you.

00:37:25.130 --> 00:37:26.430
Got it?

00:37:26.430 --> 00:37:27.930
Can you eat the apple?

00:37:27.930 --> 00:37:28.927
- [Student] Yes.

00:37:28.927 --> 00:37:29.870
- Yes, you can.

00:37:29.870 --> 00:37:31.160
You can eat the Buddha's finger,

00:37:31.160 --> 00:37:34.602
whatever it was that he
was emanating as the apple.

00:37:34.602 --> 00:37:35.880
All right, you can eat it.

00:37:35.880 --> 00:37:38.620
You can experience karmic results.

00:37:38.620 --> 00:37:42.677
Even though the whole process
is not what you thought.

00:37:42.677 --> 00:37:45.887
Because the Buddha can emanate.

00:37:45.887 --> 00:37:48.114
Now, how deep you go

00:37:48.114 --> 00:37:53.114
in that comparison is up to you.

00:37:53.603 --> 00:37:57.152
If you are tantric practitioner,

00:37:57.152 --> 00:38:00.228
it's an interesting question.

00:38:00.228 --> 00:38:02.490
All the things that ever happened to you,

00:38:02.490 --> 00:38:04.780
from all the karma you ever did,

00:38:04.780 --> 00:38:07.961
how are you supposed to think about it?

00:38:07.961 --> 00:38:10.301
That's a another question.

00:38:10.301 --> 00:38:13.388
For you Medicine Buddha practitioners.

00:38:13.388 --> 00:38:15.610
Let's stop there, we got
one more class to go.

00:38:15.610 --> 00:38:18.823
We're going to review
this whole course. Yay!

